  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nThe extended forecast continues to trend drier and cooler as the \nupper trough continues to lift northward, while a small disturbance \nbecomes near stationary over the Big Country region. Meanwhile to \nour west, we will see the upper level high center across the \nSWCONUS, which will help promote northerly flow aloft across the \nregion. On top of this, the cooler air mass in place from Thursday's \nFROPA will remain in place through the weekend with highs steady in \nthe 60s and 70s area-wide.A slight uptick in temperatures is \nexpected by early next week, as geopotential heights rise in \nresponse to a weak ridge building across the area.",
